  "<a href=\"#chain\">Chain and addresses</a>": "<a href=\"#chain\">链与地址</a>",
  "<a href=\"#contracts\">The contracts</a>": "<a href=\"#contracts\">合约</a>",
  "<a href=\"#audit\">The audit</a>": "<a href=\"#audit\">审计</a>",
  "<div class=\"rt-side-h\">Legal</div>": "<div class=\"rt-side-h\">法律</div>",
  "<a href=\"#who\">Who can invest</a>": "<a href=\"#who\">谁可以投资</a>",
  "<a href=\"#legal\">What this is, and is not</a>": "<a href=\"#legal\">这是什么，不是什么</a>",
  "A vault that owns a share of rented apartments, publishes what every one of them paid,\n      and lets you check the arithmetic.": "一个持有出租公寓份额的金库，公布每一套公寓付了多少钱，\n      并让你自己核对算术。",
  "Tenants pay rent. The bills come out of it. What is left stays in the vault and lifts the\n      price of a share. You never receive a rent transfer, and you never own an apartment.": "租客交租。账单从中扣除。剩下的留在金库里，推高份额价格。\n      你永远不会收到租金转账，也永远不会拥有一套公寓。",
  "On the first of every month the vault publishes <b>The Roll</b> — the report for the month\n      just ended. It lists every apartment, what its lease says, whether the rent arrived, and\n      every cost that was taken out. The file is hashed and the hash is written on chain beside\n      that month's closing share price, so the document you read is provably the document that\n      was published.": "每月一号，金库发布<b>月报（The Roll）</b>——刚结束那个月的报告。它列出每一套公寓、\n      租约上写的金额、租金是否到账，以及扣除的每一项成本。文件会被哈希，哈希与当月的\n      结算份额价格一起写在链上，因此你读到的文件可以被证明就是发布的那份文件。",
  "<p>These docs cover three things:</p>": "<p>本文档涵盖三件事：</p>",
  "<li><a href=\"#how\">Using the vault</a> — what a share is, how its price moves, what it costs, and what can go wrong.</li>": "<li><a href=\"#how\">使用金库</a>——份额是什么，它的价格如何变动，费用是什么，以及可能出什么问题。</li>",
  "<li><a href=\"#reading\">The Roll</a> — how to read a monthly report and how to verify one yourself.</li>": "<li><a href=\"#reading\">月报</a>——如何阅读月报，以及如何自己验证一份月报。</li>",
  "<li><a href=\"#local\">Building on it</a> — the contracts, the chain, the audit, and how to run the whole thing on your own machine.</li>": "<li><a href=\"#local\">在其上构建</a>——合约、链、审计，以及如何在自己的机器上运行整个系统。</li>",
  "<h2>The short version</h2>": "<h2>简短版本</h2>",
  "<tr><th>What you hold</th><td>vRENTA, an ERC-4626 share of the vault</td></tr>": "<tr><th>你持有什么</th><td>vRENTA，金库的 ERC-4626 份额</td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>What sets its price</th><td>The EURG the vault holds plus what its buildings are carried at, divided by the shares outstanding</td></tr>": "<tr><th>什么决定它的价格</th><td>金库持有的 EURG 加上楼宇的账面价值，除以流通份额数</td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Where the money comes from</th><td>Rent collected, net of property costs and the management fee</td></tr>": "<tr><th>钱从哪里来</th><td>实收租金，扣除物业成本和管理费</td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>When you get paid</th><td>When you redeem. There is no monthly payout.</td></tr>": "<tr><th>什么时候拿到钱</th><td>赎回时。没有月度分红。</td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>What it costs</th><td>Nothing to deposit, nothing to redeem. A curve tax if you leave within ninety days, and it stays in the vault.</td></tr>": "<tr><th>费用是什么</th><td>存入免费，赎回免费。九十天内离开需付曲线税，且它留在金库里。</td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>How you check it</th><td>Recompute the Roll's hash and compare it with the chain</td></tr>": "<tr><th>如何核对</th><td>重新计算月报的哈希，与链上的比对</td></tr>",
  "Nothing here is a projection. Every figure on the site is computed from the ledger it is\n      published with, which is why a Roll can be checked line by line rather than taken on trust.": "这里没有任何预测。网站上的每一个数字都由随之发布的账本计算得出，\n      所以一份月报可以逐行核对，而不必凭信任接受。",
  "<h2 id=\"how\">How it works</h2>": "<h2 id=\"how\">它如何运作</h2>",
  "The vault is a holding company with a token in front of it. The company — a Dutch B.V. —\n      owns ten apartment buildings outright, in eight cities across six countries, and it owns a\n      cash reserve in EURG. The token, vRENTA, is a claim on all of it in proportion.": "金库是一家控股公司，前面放着一个代币。这家公司——一家荷兰 B.V.——全款持有\n      六个国家八座城市的十栋公寓楼，并持有一笔 EURG 现金储备。代币 vRENTA 是对这一切\n      按比例的权利主张。",
  "<p>Each month, three things happen, in order:</p>": "<p>每个月，依次发生三件事：</p>",
  "<li><b>Rent is collected.</b> The managing agents in each city collect rent from seventy-seven apartments and forward it, net of their own fee, to the vault's operating account.</li>": "<li><b>收租。</b>各城市的管理机构从七十七套公寓收取租金，扣除自己的费用后转入金库的运营账户。</li>",
  "<li><b>The bills are paid.</b> Repairs, property tax, insurance, the agents and the auditor come out of that account. Whatever is left is <i>kept</i>.</li>": "<li><b>付账单。</b>维修、房产税、保险、管理机构和审计师的费用从该账户支出。剩下的即为<i>留存</i>。</li>",
  "<li><b>The close is written.</b> On the last day of the month the kept amount is added to the vault's holdings, the new share price is computed, and the Roll is published with its hash on chain.</li>": "<li><b>写入结算。</b>每月最后一天，留存金额计入金库持有量，计算新的份额价格，并发布月报，其哈希写在链上。</li>",
  "There is no borrowing anywhere in the structure. No mortgage on any building, no credit line\n      at the vault, no leverage in the token. The vault grows at the speed of deposits and retained\n      rent, which is slower than a bank would let it, and that is the point.": "这个结构里没有任何借贷。任何楼宇都没有房贷，金库没有信用额度，代币没有杠杆。\n      金库以存款和留存租金的速度增长，比银行允许的要慢，而这正是重点。",
  "<h2 id=\"price\">What sets the share price</h2>": "<h2 id=\"price\">什么决定份额价格</h2>",
  "The price of one vRENTA is what the vault holds, divided by the number of shares in issue.\n      What the vault holds is the sum of two things: the EURG in its reserve, and the buildings at\n      the value they were bought for, adjusted only when a building is sold or an independent\n      valuation is commissioned — which happens once a year, and is itself published.": "一个 vRENTA 的价格，是金库的持有量除以流通份额数。金库的持有量是两项之和：\n      储备中的 EURG，以及按买入价计的楼宇，后者只在楼宇出售或委托独立估值时调整——\n      估值每年一次，估值本身也会公布。",
  "Because the buildings are carried at cost between valuations, the price moves for exactly two\n      reasons between closes:": "由于两次估值之间楼宇按成本入账，价格在两次结算之间只因两个原因变动：",
  "<li><b>Rent kept.</b> The month's collected rent, less the month's costs, is added to the reserve.</li>": "<li><b>留存租金。</b>当月实收租金减去当月成本，计入储备。</li>",
  "<li><b>The curve tax.</b> Anyone redeeming within ninety days of a deposit sells slightly below the share price. The difference stays in the reserve for everyone else. See <a href=\"#fees\">Fees</a>.</li>": "<li><b>曲线税。</b>存入后九十天内赎回的人，以略低于份额价格的价格卖出。差额留在储备中归其他人所有。见<a href=\"#fees\">费用</a>。</li>",
  "<p>Here is the close of 31 August 2026, the sixth since the vault opened:</p>": "<p>这是 2026 年 8 月 31 日的结算，金库开放以来的第六次：</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"deposit\">Depositing and redeeming</h2>": "<h2 id=\"deposit\">存入与赎回</h2>",
  "The vault is an ERC-4626 contract, so it works the way every other one does. You approve\n      EURG, you call <code>deposit</code>, and vRENTA arrives in the same transaction at the share\n      price standing at that block. The minimum is 100 EURG. There is no maximum, no whitelist and\n      no lock-up.": "金库是一个 ERC-4626 合约，所以它的运作方式和其他合约一样。你授权 EURG，\n      调用 <code>deposit</code>，vRENTA 在同一笔交易中按该区块时的份额价格到账。\n      最低 100 EURG。没有上限，没有白名单，没有锁定期。",
  "To leave you call <code>redeem</code> with the number of shares. EURG arrives in the same\n      block as long as the reserve covers it — and the reserve is kept at roughly a month of rent\n      plus whatever redemptions are usual, which was <!-- data:reserve -->€430,593<!-- /data:reserve --> at the last close. A redemption larger\n      than the reserve is queued and settled at the next close, at that close's price. It is the\n      one case where you wait, and the Roll records every queued redemption and the day it settled.": "离开时，你带上份额数量调用 <code>redeem</code>。只要储备够付，EURG 在同一个区块到账——\n      储备大致保持在一个月租金加上通常的赎回量，上次结算时为 <!-- data:reserve -->€430,593<!-- /data:reserve -->。\n      超过储备的赎回会排队，在下一次结算时按那次结算的价格清算。这是唯一需要等待的情况，\n      月报会记录每一笔排队的赎回及其清算日期。",
  "<p><b>You never receive rent.</b> Nothing is streamed, airdropped or claimable. The rent is in the price. If you want it in your wallet, redeem the part of your holding that is worth what you want.</p>": "<p><b>你永远不会收到租金。</b>没有流式支付、空投或可领取的东西。租金在价格里。如果你想让它进钱包，就赎回你持仓中价值相当的那一部分。</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"fees\">Fees</h2>": "<h2 id=\"fees\">费用</h2>",
  "<tr><th>Deposit</th><td><span class=\"rt-num\">0.00%</span></td></tr>": "<tr><th>存入</th><td><span class=\"rt-num\">0.00%</span></td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Redeem</th><td><span class=\"rt-num\">0.00%</span></td></tr>": "<tr><th>赎回</th><td><span class=\"rt-num\">0.00%</span></td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Curve tax</th><td>On redemptions within 90 days of the most recent deposit, on a straight line from <span class=\"rt-num\">3.0%</span> on day one to <span class=\"rt-num\">0.0%</span> on day ninety. It is not a fee we collect: it stays in the vault and lifts the price for the holders who stayed.</td></tr>": "<tr><th>曲线税</th><td>适用于最近一次存入后 90 天内的赎回，从第一天的 <span class=\"rt-num\">3.0%</span> 直线下降到第九十天的 <span class=\"rt-num\">0.0%</span>。这不是我们收取的费用：它留在金库里，推高留下来的持有人的价格。</td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Management</th><td><span class=\"rt-num\">0.35%</span> of what the vault holds, a year, taken monthly out of rent before the close. It is inside the €18,250 of costs above, and it is a line in every Roll.</td></tr>": "<tr><th>管理费</th><td>每年为金库持有量的 <span class=\"rt-num\">0.35%</span>，每月在结算前从租金中扣除。它包含在上面 €18,250 的成本里，并且是每份月报中的一行。</td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Performance</th><td>None.</td></tr>": "<tr><th>业绩费</th><td>无。</td></tr>",
  "The curve tax exists so that a nervous week cannot force the vault to sell a building to pay\n      people who arrived three weeks ago. Buildings take months to sell and sell badly in a hurry;\n      the tax makes leaving early cost about what a hurried sale would have cost everyone else.": "曲线税的存在，是为了让一个紧张的星期不至于迫使金库卖掉一栋楼，去付钱给三周前才进来的人。\n      楼宇要几个月才能卖掉，而且急着卖会卖得很差；这项税让提前离开的代价，\n      大致等于一次仓促出售会让其他所有人付出的代价。",
  "<h2 id=\"risk\">What can go wrong</h2>": "<h2 id=\"risk\">可能出什么问题</h2>",
  "<p>Property is slow and it is not free of risk. In roughly the order you should worry about them:</p>": "<p>房产是慢的，也并非没有风险。大致按你应该担心的顺序：</p>",
  "<li><b>A tenant stops paying.</b> The agent chases it, the Roll records it as scheduled but not collected, and that month's price rises by less. Across seventy-seven apartments one empty flat costs a few hundred euros a month, not everything.</li>": "<li><b>租客不交租。</b>管理机构追讨，月报记为应收未收，当月价格涨幅变小。在七十七套公寓里，一套空置每月只损失几百欧元，而不是全部。</li>",
  "<li><b>A big repair.</b> A roof, a boiler, a façade. May 2026 was one: €4,180 on Kurt-Eisner-Straße, paid once, out of that month's rent. The price still rose that month, by a little less.</li>": "<li><b>一次大修。</b>屋顶、锅炉、外墙。2026 年 5 月就有一次：Kurt-Eisner-Straße 花了 €4,180，一次付清，从当月租金里出。那个月价格照样上涨，只是少了一点。</li>",
  "<li><b>A valuation falls.</b> Once a year the buildings are revalued independently. If a market has fallen, the price of a share falls with it on that close. This is the only way the price goes down other than a redemption queue being settled below reserve.</li>": "<li><b>估值下跌。</b>楼宇每年独立重估一次。如果某个市场跌了，份额价格在那次结算时随之下跌。除了赎回队列以低于储备的价格清算之外，这是价格下跌的唯一途径。</li>",
  "<li><b>A redemption queue.</b> If redemptions exceed the reserve, they wait for the next close. In an extreme case the vault would sell a building to meet them, at whatever the market gives, and everyone's share would carry that.</li>": "<li><b>赎回队列。</b>如果赎回超过储备，它们要等到下一次结算。极端情况下金库会卖掉一栋楼来应付，市场给什么价就是什么价，每个人的份额都要承担这一点。</li>",
  "<li><b>The stablecoin.</b> The vault holds EURG. If EURG were to trade away from one euro, the reserve would be worth less in euros even though nothing about the buildings changed.</li>": "<li><b>稳定币。</b>金库持有 EURG。如果 EURG 的交易价格偏离一欧元，即使楼宇没有任何变化，储备按欧元计也会缩水。</li>",
  "<li><b>Us.</b> The company that runs the vault could stop. The holding company and the buildings do not depend on it: vRENTA holders own the holding company, the vault contract accepts redemptions from any wallet whether or not this site exists, and the deeds are registered in the ordinary way in each country.</li>": "<li><b>我们。</b>运营金库的公司可能会停止。控股公司和楼宇不依赖它：vRENTA 持有人拥有控股公司，无论这个网站是否存在，金库合约都接受任何钱包的赎回，房契也在各国以常规方式登记。</li>",
  "<h2 id=\"reading\">Reading a Roll</h2>": "<h2 id=\"reading\">阅读月报</h2>",
  "A Roll is one month of the vault, in full, in one file. It has four parts, and they are\n      always in this order:": "一份月报是金库一个月的全部内容，装在一个文件里。它有四个部分，顺序永远如下：",
  "<li><b>The header.</b> The month, the opening and closing share price, the shares in issue at open and close, and the hash of the previous Roll.</li>": "<li><b>头部。</b>月份、期初和期末份额价格、期初和期末的流通份额数，以及上一份月报的哈希。</li>",
  "<li><b>The rent roll proper.</b> One line per apartment: building, unit, what the lease says is due, what arrived and on which day, and a note if it was late, partial or missing.</li>": "<li><b>租金表本身。</b>每套公寓一行：楼宇、单元、租约上应付的金额、到账金额和到账日，以及晚付、部分付或未付的备注。</li>",
  "<li><b>The costs.</b> Every payment out of the operating account, with the building it belongs to, the payee, the invoice reference and the amount. The management fee is a line here like any other.</li>": "<li><b>成本。</b>运营账户的每一笔支出，附所属楼宇、收款方、发票编号和金额。管理费在这里和其他项一样是一行。</li>",
  "<li><b>The movements.</b> Every deposit and redemption in the month, by wallet, with the price it was struck at and any curve tax applied.</li>": "<li><b>资金变动。</b>当月每一笔存入和赎回，按钱包列出，附成交价格和适用的曲线税。</li>",
  "The two numbers people read first are <b>scheduled</b> and <b>collected</b>. Scheduled is what\n      the leases say. Collected is what arrived. The gap between them is the month's story, and the\n      rent roll tells it line by line.": "大家最先看的两个数字是<b>应收</b>和<b>实收</b>。应收是租约上写的。实收是到账的。\n      两者的差距就是这个月的故事，租金表逐行讲述它。",
  "<h2 id=\"verifying\">Verifying a Roll</h2>": "<h2 id=\"verifying\">验证月报</h2>",
  "A Roll is published as a plain file, and its SHA-256 hash is written to the vault contract\n      by the same transaction that sets the month's closing price. To check one:": "月报以纯文件形式发布，其 SHA-256 哈希由设置当月结算价格的同一笔交易写入金库合约。\n      验证一份月报：",
  "<span class=\"c\"># fetch the Roll for August 2026 and hash it</span>": "<span class=\"c\"># 下载 2026 年 8 月的月报并计算哈希</span>",
  "<span class=\"c\"># read the hash the registry holds for that close</span>": "<span class=\"c\"># 读取登记合约为该次结算保存的哈希</span>",
  "<span class=\"c\"># they should match. If they do not, the file you have is not the one published.</span>": "<span class=\"c\"># 两者应当一致。若不一致，你手里的文件不是发布的那份。</span>",
  "<span class=\"c\"># or let the script do all six, and recompute every close while it is at it</span>": "<span class=\"c\"># 或者让脚本一次处理六份，顺便重算每一次结算</span>",
  "<p>Every Roll published so far, with the hash the registry holds for it:</p>": "<p>迄今发布的每一份月报，及登记合约为其保存的哈希：</p>",
  "Then recompute the close. Sum the collected column, subtract the costs, divide by the shares\n      in issue at the close, add the curve tax per share from the movements, and add the result to\n      the opening price. You should land on the closing price in the header to six decimals. A\n      small script that does this for every Roll since the vault opened is in the repository.": "然后重算结算。把实收列求和，减去成本，除以结算时的流通份额数，加上资金变动中的\n      每份额曲线税，再把结果加到期初价格上。你应该得到头部中精确到小数点后六位的结算价格。\n      仓库里有一个小脚本，对金库开放以来的每一份月报都做这件事。",
  "<h2 id=\"format\">The published file format</h2>": "<h2 id=\"format\">发布文件的格式</h2>",
  "One CSV per month, UTF-8, comma separated, with a <code>section</code> column that takes one\n      of <code>header</code>, <code>rent</code>, <code>cost</code> or <code>movement</code>. Amounts\n      are in EURG with six decimals and no thousands separators. Dates are ISO 8601. Wallets are\n      checksummed. Nothing in the file is derived from anything outside the file except the\n      previous Roll's hash.": "每月一个 CSV，UTF-8，逗号分隔，带一个 <code>section</code> 列，取值为\n      <code>header</code>、<code>rent</code>、<code>cost</code> 或 <code>movement</code> 之一。\n      金额以 EURG 计，六位小数，无千位分隔符。日期为 ISO 8601。钱包地址带校验和。\n      除上一份月报的哈希外，文件中没有任何内容来自文件之外。",
  "<h2 id=\"local\">Run it locally</h2>": "<h2 id=\"local\">在本地运行</h2>",
  "The site is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript with no build step. The contracts are Foundry.\n      Everything on the site is computed from the Rolls, so with the Rolls on disk you can\n      reproduce every number on it without touching the chain.": "网站是纯 HTML、CSS 和 JavaScript，没有构建步骤。合约用 Foundry。\n      网站上的一切都由月报计算得出，所以只要月报在磁盘上，你不用碰链就能重现每一个数字。",
  "<span class=\"c\"># the site</span>": "<span class=\"c\"># 网站</span>",
  "<span class=\"c\"># the contracts</span>": "<span class=\"c\"># 合约</span>",
  "<span class=\"c\"># recompute every close from the Rolls</span>": "<span class=\"c\"># 从月报重算每一次结算</span>",
  "<h2 id=\"chain\">Chain and addresses</h2>": "<h2 id=\"chain\">链与地址</h2>",
  "The vault runs on an Ethereum L2. EURG is a euro-denominated stablecoin issued under an EU\n      e-money licence and redeemable one-for-one. The addresses below are for the demonstration\n      deployment; the live ones will be listed here, and only here, when there are any.": "金库运行在一条以太坊 L2 上。EURG 是一种以欧元计价的稳定币，在欧盟电子货币牌照下发行，\n      可一比一赎回。下面的地址属于演示部署；正式地址一旦存在，将在这里、也只在这里列出。",
  "<tr><th>Vault (vRENTA)</th><td><code>0x5A1c…e8f4</code></td></tr>": "<tr><th>金库（vRENTA）</th><td><code>0x5A1c…e8f4</code></td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Asset (EURG)</th><td><code>0xE0d2…71b9</code></td></tr>": "<tr><th>资产（EURG）</th><td><code>0xE0d2…71b9</code></td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Roll registry</th><td><code>0x9b7F…03ad</code></td></tr>": "<tr><th>月报登记合约</th><td><code>0x9b7F…03ad</code></td></tr>",
  "<tr><th>Holding company</th><td>RENTA Vastgoed B.V., Rotterdam — KvK number published with the first live Roll</td></tr>": "<tr><th>控股公司</th><td>RENTA Vastgoed B.V.，鹿特丹——KvK 注册号将随第一份正式月报公布</td></tr>",
  "<h2 id=\"contracts\">The contracts</h2>": "<h2 id=\"contracts\">合约</h2>",
  "<p>There are three, and they are small on purpose.</p>": "<p>一共三个，而且刻意写得很小。</p>",
  "<li><b>Vault.</b> An ERC-4626 with two additions: a curve on <code>redeem</code> that looks up the caller's most recent deposit, and a <code>close</code> function that only the operator can call, once a month, which sets the new price and the Roll's hash together. The price cannot be set without a hash, and a hash cannot be set without a price.</li>": "<li><b>Vault。</b>一个 ERC-4626，加了两样东西：<code>redeem</code> 上的曲线，它会查找调用者最近一次存入；以及一个只有运营方可以每月调用一次的 <code>close</code> 函数，它同时设置新价格和月报哈希。没有哈希就设不了价格，没有价格也设不了哈希。</li>",
  "<li><b>Roll registry.</b> A map from month to hash, append-only. Once written, a month's hash cannot be changed by anyone, including us.</li>": "<li><b>月报登记合约。</b>一个从月份到哈希的映射，只能追加。一旦写入，某月的哈希任何人都改不了，包括我们。</li>",
  "<li><b>Operator.</b> A two-of-three multisig that holds the right to call <code>close</code>. It has no right to move EURG out of the vault; only <code>redeem</code> can do that, and only to the redeeming wallet.</li>": "<li><b>运营方。</b>一个三取二多签，拥有调用 <code>close</code> 的权利。它无权把 EURG 转出金库；只有 <code>redeem</code> 能做到，而且只能转给赎回的钱包。</li>",
  "The source is in the repository, verified on the explorer, and it does not upgrade. If a\n      change is ever needed it will be a new vault, announced in a Roll, with a migration you opt\n      into.": "源代码在仓库里，在区块浏览器上已验证，并且不可升级。如果将来需要改动，那会是一个新金库，\n      在月报中公布，并提供一个由你自行选择是否参与的迁移。",
  "<h2 id=\"audit\">The audit</h2>": "<h2 id=\"audit\">审计</h2>",
  "Two things are audited, by two different people. The contracts were reviewed by an\n      independent smart-contract firm before deployment, and the report is in the repository with\n      every finding and what was done about it. The company's accounts — the buildings, the rent,\n      the bank balances — are audited annually by a registered Dutch auditor, and the audited\n      accounts are published beside the December Roll. The Roll's job is to make the second audit\n      boring: by the time the auditor arrives, twelve months of the ledger have already been\n      public and hashed.": "有两样东西被审计，由两个不同的人来做。合约在部署前由一家独立的智能合约公司审阅，\n      报告在仓库里，附每一项发现及其处理。公司的账目——楼宇、租金、银行余额——每年由一位\n      注册的荷兰审计师审计，经审计的账目随十二月的月报一起发布。月报的作用是让第二项审计\n      变得无聊：审计师到来时，十二个月的账本早已公开并哈希过了。",
  "<h2 id=\"who\">Who can invest</h2>": "<h2 id=\"who\">谁可以投资</h2>",
  "vRENTA is offered to people resident in the EU and EEA, Switzerland and the United Kingdom,\n      who are 18 or over and who pass an identity check. It is not offered to residents or\n      citizens of the United States, Canada or Japan, nor anywhere that would require a licence\n      the company does not hold, nor to anyone on an EU sanctions list. The list is in\n      <code>config.js</code> and on the gate you see before connecting a wallet.": "vRENTA 面向居住在欧盟和欧洲经济区、瑞士和英国、年满 18 岁并通过身份验证的人发售。\n      不面向美国、加拿大或日本的居民或公民，不面向任何需要公司尚未持有的牌照的地方，\n      也不面向欧盟制裁名单上的任何人。名单在 <code>config.js</code> 里，也在连接钱包前\n      看到的那道门上。",
  "The identity check is run by a regulated provider and happens once, before your first\n      deposit. The vault contract itself does not know who you are — it knows a wallet — and\n      the company keeps the link between the two under EU data-protection law, for as long as\n      anti-money-laundering rules require and no longer.": "身份验证由受监管的服务商执行，在你第一次存入前进行一次。金库合约本身不知道你是谁——\n      它只认识一个钱包——公司依照欧盟数据保护法保存两者之间的关联，保存期限以反洗钱规则\n      要求为限，不会更长。",
  "<h2 id=\"legal\">What this is, and is not</h2>": "<h2 id=\"legal\">这是什么，不是什么</h2>",
  "vRENTA is a share of a company that owns buildings. In most places that makes it a\n      security, and it is offered as one. It is not a deposit, it is not insured, and its price\n      can fall. Rent can stop arriving. A building can be worth less next year than it was this\n      year. Past closes are a record, not a promise.": "vRENTA 是一家持有楼宇的公司的份额。在大多数地方这使它成为一种证券，它也是作为证券发售的。\n      它不是存款，没有保险，价格可能下跌。租金可能停止到账。一栋楼明年可能比今年更不值钱。\n      过去的结算是记录，不是承诺。",
  "Nothing on this site or in these docs is advice. If you would not buy a share of a small\n      property company on the strength of its published accounts, do not buy this on the strength\n      of a Roll.": "本网站和本文档中的任何内容都不是建议。如果你不会仅凭一家小型房产公司公布的账目去买它的股份，\n      也不要仅凭一份月报来买这个。",
  "<p><b>This is a demonstration build.</b> Every address, every building and every close on this site is invented to show how the mechanism reads. There is no wallet connector, no deployed contract and no company behind it.</p>": "<p><b>这是一个演示版本。</b>本网站上的每一个地址、每一栋楼和每一次结算都是虚构的，用来展示这套机制读起来是什么样。背后没有已部署的合约，也没有公司。</p>",
  "<p>A share of the rent, without the building, the mortgage or the phone call at six in the morning.</p>": "<p>一份租金，没有楼、没有房贷，也没有早上六点的电话。</p>",
  "<div class=\"rt-fcol-h\">Read</div>": "<div class=\"rt-fcol-h\">阅读</div>",
  "<div class=\"rt-fcol-h\">Onchain</div>": "<div class=\"rt-fcol-h\">链上</div>",
  ">Deposit EURG</a>": ">存入 EURG</a>",
  ">Documentation</a>": ">文档</a>",
  ">Explorer</a>": ">区块浏览器</a>",
  ">Vault contract</a>": ">金库合约</a>",
  ">Audit</a>": ">审计</a>",
  "RENTA is a demonstration build. Every figure on this page is illustrative, and past\n        closes are not a promise about future ones. Property can fall in value and rent can\n        stop arriving. Nothing here is investment advice.": "RENTA 是一个演示版本。本页所有数字仅作示意，过去的结算不构成对未来的承诺。\n        房产可能贬值，租金可能停止到账。这里没有任何内容是投资建议。",
  "aria-label=\"RENTA on X (Twitter)\"": "aria-label=\"RENTA 的 X（Twitter）\"",
  ">Sandbox</a>": ">沙盒</a>"
}
